course: dictionary
lesson: 10606
title: Undocumented: not written down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undocumented means not written down or recorded anywhere. The prefix un- means not, and document is a written record, so undocumented is the opposite of documented. «Undocumented feature» is a joking name for a software bug, because it is a feature that is not in the instructions.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. «Programmers joke that a bug is an "undocumented feature", and a firm that lost a fortune may call it "a learning experience".» The joke works because a bug was never written in the instructions. Swap in your meaning: "a bug that is not written down in the instructions" still makes sense.
explain: The same word can be used for people. «Undocumented immigrant» means a person living in a country without the official papers that allow them to be there. It is a polite, respectful term, a softer word than "illegal".
fact: Undocumented means not written down or recorded anywhere.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so undocumented is the opposite of documented.
fact: «Undocumented feature» means a feature that is not in the instructions; programmers often use it as a joking name for a bug.
fact: In history, «undocumented» events are events with no written record.
fact: «Undocumented immigrant» means a person living in a country without official papers; it is a polite term.
exercise: «Programmers joke that a bug is an "undocumented feature".» What does undocumented mean here? | Broken for ever | *Not written down in the instructions | Very easy to use | Printed in colour
exercise: «The battle is undocumented, so historians know little about it.» Find and copy the word that tells you nothing was written down. | *undocumented | battle | little | historians
exercise: In undocumented, the prefix un- means what? | *Not | Very | Again | Under
test: «The old village has an undocumented history.» What does this mean? | Has a written record of every day | *Has no written record | Is near the sea | Is very famous
test: Why is «undocumented immigrant» called a polite term? | It is a type of computer bug | It means the person has lots of papers | It means the person is very rich | *It is a softer, more respectful way to describe the person
exam: Which word means not written down or recorded anywhere? | Documented | Written | Famous | *Undocumented
